      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Cypher sits at an interesting intersection between corporate thriller and science fiction, alongside films like <a href=\"/movie/9886\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9886\">Johnny Mnemonic</a> (1995) and <a href=\"/movie/281\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"281\">Strange Days</a> (1995). Its exploration of memory manipulation and corporate control feels particularly relevant in our era of data mining and surveillance capitalism. The film's themes of identity erasure and corporate conformity echo through later works like <a href=\"/movie/45612\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"45612\">Source Code</a> (2011) and <a href=\"/movie/1635\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1635\">The Island</a> (2005), though with more subtlety and psychological depth."
      }
